<title>ISRAEL: Shekem net down, operating loss narrows.</title>
<headline>Shekem net down, operating loss narrows.</headline>
<dateline>TEL AVIV 1997-05-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shekem Ltd, a subsidiary of Elco Holdings Ltd, reported the following results.</p>
<p>			 (in thousands of shekels)</p>
<p>				Q1 97	Q1 96</p>
<p>Sales			 206,892    303,332</p>
<p>Operating income (loss) (10,950)   (14,136)</p>
<p>Other income		 11,439     41,025</p>
<p>Pretax income		 1,080     27,824</p>
<p>Net income		    1,045     25,362</p>
<p>The decline in Shekem's sales was mainly due to the December 31 sale of its supermarket chain, said Elco managing director Uri Kviatek.</p>
<p>Shekem's operating loss was the smallest in the past five quarters. Despite this, net income declined in the first quarter compared with the year-earlier quarter because capital gains from the sale of property were greater in the first quarter of 1996 than in the first quarter of 1997, Kviatek said.</p>
<p>($1=3.40 shekels)</p>
<p>-Tel Aviv newsroom, 972-3-537-2211</p>
